Problem:
Let $x, y, z$ be nonnegative real numbers such that $x + y + z = 9$. Define
\begin{align*}
C &= \sqrt{x + 3} + \sqrt{y + 6} + \sqrt{z + 12}, \\
D &= \sqrt{x + 2} + \sqrt{y + 2} + \sqrt{z + 2}.
\end{align*}
Find the minimum value of $C^2 - D^2$.

Find all real number pairs \((x, y)\) that satisfy:
$$
\left\{
\begin{array}{l}
x^{2}+y^{2}+x+y=xy(x+y)-\frac{10}{27}, \\
|xy| \leq \frac{25}{9}.
\end{array}
\right.
$$
